Subject: [PATCH] Keep architecture-specific clamp result types local

The pinned compiler 6a7a7c531f54baed1dddfda1b80299413c4c6943 defines
ClampIntersectionResult at global scope in NPU37XX and NPU50XX, with
incompatible field types. GCC 16.2.1 reproduces the One Definition Rule
violation when linking the two real objects with LTO.

Give each private result type translation-unit identity. Preserve all fields,
clamp arithmetic and call sites. No warning option is disabled.
Regression: check-clamp-odr.py links the actual built objects with strict LTO
ODR diagnostics. The original objects fail; objects must retain LTO metadata.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/NPU37XX/dialect/VPU/impl/ppe_factory.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/NPU37XX/dialect/VPU/impl/ppe_factory.cpp
@@ -130,11 +130,15 @@
     }
 }
 
+namespace {
+
 struct ClampIntersectionResult {
     int32_t low;
     int32_t high;
     PPEMode mode;
 };
+
+}  // namespace
 
 static ClampIntersectionResult calcClampIntersection(const int32_t currentLow, const int32_t currentHigh,
                                                      const double newLow, const double newHigh,
--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/NPU50XX/dialect/VPU/impl/ppe_factory.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/NPU50XX/dialect/VPU/impl/ppe_factory.cpp
@@ -305,12 +305,16 @@
     }
 }
 
+namespace {
+
 struct ClampIntersectionResult {
     double low;
     double high;
     PPEMode mode;
     double adder;
 };
+
+}  // namespace
 
 static ClampIntersectionResult calcClampIntersection(const double currentLow, const double currentHigh,
                                                      const double newLow, const double newHigh,
